Algorithm:

1. Start.
2. Define a node structure for the binary tree.
3. Create the binary tree with left and right child pointers.
4. Traverse each node of the binary tree.
5. Check whether each node has zero, one, or two children.
6. If any node has exactly one child, mark the tree as not a full binary tree.
7. If every node has either zero or two children, mark the tree as a full binary tree.
8. Display whether the given binary tree is full or not.
9. Stop.
